# Files you must NOT edit

Cursor has no PreToolUse hook to enforce this mechanically (Claude
Code blocks edits via `.claude/hooks/block_protected_files.sh`).
The rule is on you:

- **`uv.lock`** — managed by `uv add` / `uv lock`. Manual edits diverge
  the lockfile from the resolver and break reproducibility. To add a
  dep, run `uv add <pkg>`. To upgrade, run `uv lock --upgrade-package
  <pkg>` or `uv lock --upgrade` for everything.

- **`.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.<env>`, `.env.<env>.local`** — these
  contain secrets and **must not** be committed. `.env.example` is
  the only `.env*` file that is intentionally checked in and editable.
  If the change requires a new env var, document it in
  `.env.example` (and in `docs/deployment-variables.md`).

If a refactor or rename would *appear* to require editing one of
these files, stop and re-think — the right path almost always lives
through `uv add` / `uv sync` for the lockfile, or `.env.example` plus
`docs/deployment-variables.md` for env vars.
